      "attrs": {
        "text": "You are reviewing one task's implementation: first whether it matches its requirements, then whether it is well-built. This is a task-scoped gate, not a merge review — a broad whole-branch review happens separately after all tasks.\n\n## What Was Requested\nRead the task brief: `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-1-brief.md`\n\nGlobal constraints from the spec that bind this task:\n- `requirements.txt` must gain exactly: `sqlalchemy>=2.0`, `alembic>=1.13`, `psycopg[binary]>=3.1` (verbatim).\n- src-layout: imports are `server.storage.*`; tests under `tests/server/storage/`.\n- No \"Claude\" / \"co-authored-by Claude\" anywhere in code or commit messages.\n- TDD required: failing test first, then implementation.\n\n## What the Implementer Claims They Built\nRead the implementer's report: `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-1-report.md`\n\n## Diff Under Review\nBase: f2cea88  Head: 9c0b8bb\nDiff file: `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/review-f2cea88..9c0b8bb.diff`\nRead the diff file once — it contains the commit list, stat summary, and full diff with context; it is your view of the change. Do not re-run git commands or crawl the codebase. Read-only: do not mutate the working tree, index, or HEAD.\n\n## Do Not Trust the Report\nTreat the report as unverified claims; verify against the diff.\n\n## Tests\nThe implementer already ran the tests with TDD evidence. Do not re-run the suite; run a focused test only if reading the code raises a specific doubt (name it if you can't run it). Warnings/noise in reported output are findings.\n\nFollow the review method and output format below.\n\n## Part 1: Spec Compliance — Missing / Extra / Misunderstood vs. the brief.\n## Part 2: Code Quality — clean separation, error handling, DRY, tests verify real behavior, structure/file responsibility. Cite file:line for every finding.\n\n## Calibration\nCategorize by actual severity. Important = task cannot be trusted until fixed (missed requirement, fragile behavior, tests that assert nothing). Polish/coverage = Minor. If the plan mandates something the rubric calls a defect, report it Important labeled plan-mandated. Acknowledge what was done well.\n\n## Output Format\n### Spec Compliance\n- ✅ Spec compliant | ❌ Issues found (with file:line) | ⚠️ Cannot verify from diff\n### Strengths\n### Issues — #### Critical / #### Important / #### Minor (each: file:line, what's wrong, why, how to fix)\n### Assessment\n**Task quality:** Approved | Needs fixes\n**Reasoning:** 1-2 sentences.\n\nYour final message is the report itself — begin directly with the spec-compliance verdict, no preamble.",
